.DS_Store
_build/
target/
target
.mooncakes/
.moonagent/
.githooks/

# `shadow/generated.mbt` is written by the `gen` rule at build time and is
# never committed: half of it comes from `moon.mod`, the other half is the git
# checkout the build ran in — commit, author, dirty flag. Baking a checkout
# into a tracked file means every build in a different checkout (CI's own, for
# one) produces a diff, which is exactly what `git diff --exit-code` in
# scripts/ci.sh is there to catch. Generated, not tracked: the build writes it
# before anything imports it, so nothing needs it in the tree.
shadow/generated.mbt


# The zip `moon package`/`moon publish` builds is cut with these same rules, so
# ignoring the generated file above also drops it from the release — and the
# registry's own `moon check` on the packed `shadow` package then fails: the
# package declares a virtual with nothing implementing it. 0.1.4 shipped the
# file (it predates the ignore lines); this keeps it shipping. The order
# matters: a later rule beats an earlier one, and `shadow/.gitignore` is
# ignored separately below.
!shadow/generated.mbt
shadow/.gitignore
